# The first module (retreat_module_spawner, from Retreat-Modules) in the sandbox: its command
# runs through the same registry, its boxes go through the engine's physics.
# Run: cargo run -p retreat_sandbox -- --headless --commands scripts/verify/module_spawner.cmds
# Expected pictures:
#   module_spawner_falling.png: blue boxes of mixed sizes in the air, the lowest about to land.
#   module_spawner_rest.png:    the blue boxes at rest on the ground and on the cube.

spawner.rain 12
# 0.8 s in: the lower boxes have fallen into view.
wait 50
snapshot module_spawner_falling
# 4.5 s more: everything lands and settles (5.3 s in total, as recorded).
wait 286
snapshot module_spawner_rest
# Positions come from SimulationRng (seed 0): the same on every platform. Some boxes are still
# settling, so the hash changes every tick: the assert's value is the one at its own line (one
# tick after the `state.hash` print), copied from its failure message when re-recording.
state.hash
assert.state_hash 0x6c0164612acaad2f
quit
